 "scope": "NJet 2.1.1 (CDR, MS-bar renormalisation, N_f = 5, no top quark) at N_c = 2, 3, 4, 5, 6 (NJetNc): MQ-NC's independent N_c oracle of the full-colour virtual (m-qcd PLAN \u00a73.2 MQ-NC (a)). gg_gg and gg_ggg: direct mode in double-double (Amp::setNc); the driver's normalisation (njet_driver.cpp, BLHA's 1/256 colour and spin average of two gluons and the identical-gluon factor) is the N_c = 3 one at every N_c. uux_ggg, uux_ddxg, uux_uuxg: NJet's BLHA interface (contract signed by njet.py with 'Extra NJetNc N', NJetMultiPrec 1 and Precision 1e-30, so every point is re-evaluated in double-double from refined momenta; the output is binary64); NJet's BLHA output divides by its initial colour average at N_c (njet.py get_colour_dof: N_c per quark, N_c^2-1 per gluon), so born, finite, single_pole and double_pole are stored times avg(N_c)/avg(3) (entry 'colour_average'; the raw NJet values under each row's 'njet'). pyAmpliCol's N_c scan keeps the request's N_c = 3 average (tests/unit/loop_nc_scan.py), so every stored value compares without a further correction. Check of the BLHA path: gg_gg and gg_ggg through BLHA at N_c = 2 and 4, so corrected, equal the direct double-double values within 3.2e-15. Produced with tools/loop_reference/njet/run_njet.py run (--mode blha --process ... --nc N) and nc-entry.",
 "convention": "MadLoop/BLHA C_eps=(4pi)^eps/Gamma(1-eps); CDR/HV ('t Hooft-Veltman) with MS-bar alpha_s(mu_R); physical couplings g_s^2=4 pi alpha_s; initial spin and colour average and final identical-gluon factor 1/5!; the virtual is 2 Re<M0|M1>. This is the convention of every tests/fixtures/loop/required fixture (MadLoop, OpenLoops truepoles=1 polenorm=0, Recola +pi^2/6 D) and of pyAmpliCol (loops/v2/conventions.py); calibrated without any factor, see calibration.",
